  0. Definitions.

  "The Program" refers to any copyrightable work licensed under this License.

  "The Software" means the TIM (Task Interference Mapping) implementation
  and associated code contained in this repository.

  "Non-Commercial Research Use" means use by academic institutions,
  individual researchers, and non-profit organizations for the purpose
  of academic research, education, and non-commercial experimentation,
  provided that no revenue is generated from the use of the Software or
  from products or services that incorporate the Software.

  "Evaluation Use" means running the diagnostic on your own models and
  tasks in order to decide whether the method is of use to you, including
  inside a for-profit organization, and reporting or publishing the result.
  It does not include placing an adapter chosen by the Software in a model
  that is deployed or offered commercially.

